From 401a2e8d29f04cda83e90c8681c3e31f32176aa5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 20:41:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] fix(steam): start the x86-64 client on ARMv8.0 CPUs, and
 cap low-tier sessions at 60 Hz

- CpuFeatures reads HWCAP_ATOMICS from /proc/self/auxv (then /proc/cpuinfo); a CPU known
  to lack it always gets the x86-64 client, the settings offer only that client with the
  reason, and a SIGILL on the arm64 client names it.
- LowTierDevice (ARMv8.0 CPU or Adreno 605-620) starts the session refresh cap at 60 Hz;
  Display settings choose 60 Hz or the panel maximum, and Reset settings clears it.
- xCloud's native player starts without DDFG frame generation there; a saved choice wins.
- The device report lists the CPU class, the Steam client in effect and the refresh cap.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
